{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Matzot, for it had not leavened.</b> That is, the reason they baked it as matzot is that it was not permitted to them to eat leaven; therefore they hastened to bake it as matzah. And even though some time elapsed from the time of kneading to the time of baking, perhaps this is because they were continually working the dough, and therefore the verse says ״their kneading troughs bound up in their garments upon their shoulders״ — and did they have no place to carry them, that they were forced to put them upon their shoulders? Rather, it was so that they would continually work them, and all the while that one works the dough it does not become leavened — in addition to the fact that they put no leaven in it. And the verse gives the reason: <b>for it had not leavened, because they were driven out of Egypt</b>, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:17.588100333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}